# THE HALF-BROKEN WALKER'S LIMP, FROM THE GROUND (ColossusDef.limp,
# colossus_walk.gd `window`): its lame leg, the one in this world's first tread,
# is longer in the air than a sound one and stops a few hundred metres over its
# crater before it plants. The straddling walker is staged 56 world minutes
# before that foot comes down. He stands off the crater's lip, the view turned
# onto the foot and tipped up: it lowers, hangs there still for half a minute
# (01 and 02, fourteen seconds apart, are one picture), then sets down (03).
#   TOUR_TIMEOUT=400 tools/tour.sh tours/colossi_hitch.tour --seed=7 --place=tread0 --colossus=2@tread0-56 --hour=12 --view=shoulder --weather=clear:0
await colossus_foot 30
at climb:lip
back here 400
mouse 640,-200 0.5
wait 1
shot 00-lowering
wait 6
shot 01-hanging
wait 10
shot 02-still-hanging
until colossus_quake 60
shot 03-down
wait 2
shot 04-the-dust
